data: {"messages":[{"content":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"f5fe0a5f-0350-4490-8dc7-7f251fb52854"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"fa8651fd-423a-4c6b-b094-c538e3f662f8"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？\n任务规划：\n1. 读取视频监控系统的事件配置表与算法日志，解析当前设定的置信度阈值参数、画面遮挡检测模块的触发逻辑及执法相关事件的自动标记规则，完成数据结构化提取。预期产出：系统触发条件清单与原始参数映射表。\n2. 依托视频监控场景的目标检测与行为识别能力，按置信度低于基线、遮挡面积占比超限、事件标签含执法属性三项维度对告警数据进行过滤与归类，建立分类判定口径。预期产出：分维度的待复核事件特征矩阵。\n3. 检索安防巡检标准作业流程与执法证据留存规范，将分类结果与合规依据进行交叉比对，识别强制复核的边界条件与潜在漏判风险。预期产出：带依据索引的复核规则对照表及合规性校验报告。\n4. 整合校验后的规则清单与操作要求，编排人工复核任务的优先级序列、处置流转路径及溯源字段，生成标准化执行指引文档。预期产出：可落地的强制人工复核任务清单与操作手册。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '', '监控目标': '', '时间范围': '', '输出形式': ''}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"1c29b81c-0454-4ae9-a8b7-1052fa09fb98"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":103,"prompt_tokens":13198,"total_tokens":13301,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":57,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":103},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13198}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-2c832405-2f60-936b-a1c4-5de839c9d8aa","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-7ae7-78b2-9079-32b3ff87d4ea-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"human-review-routing","mode":"prepare"},"id":"call_e19d9a1a18bd496a895690c2","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13198,"output_tokens":103,"total_tokens":13301,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":57}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"86bfd1cb-5020-4e7d-8027-98f4b34c69e4\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取视频监控系统的事件配置表与算法日志，解析当前设定的置信度阈值参数、画面遮挡检测模块的触发逻辑及执法相关事件的自动标记规则，完成数据结构化提取。预期产出：系统触发条件清单与原始参数映射表。\\n2. 依托视频监控场景的目标检测与行为识别能力，按置信度低于基线、遮挡面积占比超限、事件标签含执法属性三项维度对告警数据进行过滤与归类，建立分类判定口径。预期产出：分维度的待复核事件特征矩阵。\\n3. 检索安防巡检标准作业流程与执法证据留存规范，将分类结果与合规依据进行交叉比对，识别强制复核的边界条件与潜在漏判风险。预期产出：带依据索引的复核规则对照表及合规性校验报告。\\n4. 整合校验后的规则清单与操作要求，编排人工复核任务的优先级序列、处置流转路径及溯源字段，生成标准化执行指引文档。预期产出：可落地的强制人工复核任务清单与操作手册。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '', '监控目标': '', '时间范围': '', '输出形式': ''}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"human-review-routing\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"e96e6d94-77c2-4144-a4ee-4ea67b946d5e","tool_call_id":"call_e19d9a1a18bd496a895690c2","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":90,"prompt_tokens":14360,"total_tokens":14450,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":27,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":90},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14360}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-d741c383-7866-992f-9978-ee6e0dc74f8e","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-8299-7dc1-8bf6-8f4d8460b111-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取人工复核路由技能的工作流程文档","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_b996362cec4549fc8b681f3a","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14360,"output_tokens":90,"total_tokens":14450,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":27}}},{"content":"---\nname: human-review-routing\ndescription: Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.\n---\n\n# Human Review Routing\n\n## Execution Priority\n\nPrioritize calling this skill's `scripts/run.py` entrypoint first. Only write custom code after the script result is unsuitable or the script cannot cover the requested task.\n\n## Input Resolution\n\nIf event confidence or event fields are missing but the user provided a video analysis request, first call `single-video-event-analysis` to produce candidate events, then call this skill for review routing.\n\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\nRun this skill directly with its own script. The script does not call other skill scripts and does not depend on shared `src`, `tools`, or registry modules.\n\n```bash\npython human-review-routing/scripts/run.py --event-json <event.json> --camera-health-json <health.json> --config <config.json> --output <review.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--event-json`, `--camera-health-json`, `--review-threshold`, `--config`, `--output`.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Read event confidence, event type, camera health, and review threshold.\n2. Require review for low confidence, high-risk types, degraded cameras, new cameras, or enforcement impact.\n3. Return review flag, reasons, threshold, and queue.\n\n## Available Implementation\n\nThis skill is implemented as an atomic standalone script in its own `scripts/run.py`. The script contains the executable logic for this skill and must not import shared `src`, `tools`, or registry modules.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `event`\n- `camera_health`\n- Optional `review_threshold`\n\nConfig:\n- `default_review_threshold`\n- `review_thresholds.<event_type>`\n- `high_risk_event_types`\n\n## Outputs\n\nReturns `event_id`, `review_required`, `reasons`, `review_threshold`, and `queue`.\n\n## Failure Modes\n\nThe current implementation tolerates missing optional config and falls back to threshold `0.85`.\n\n## Constraints\n\nDo not merge duplicate events or generate evidence.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"9aace99d-8820-4110-a183-f8309d7a205a","tool_call_id":"call_b996362cec4549fc8b681f3a","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":177,"prompt_tokens":14912,"total_tokens":15089,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":120,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":177},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14912}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-e48836b1-7243-9d9e-a191-b6ff0e28a72b","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-aab8-7c00-a3b4-5fff706e1f35-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ls","args":{"description":"查看人工复核技能目录结构","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing"},"id":"call_0f42c6d755ff48ad92a92db8","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14912,"output_tokens":177,"total_tokens":15089,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":120}}},{"content":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/run.py\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/__pycache__\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/router_card.json","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"ls","id":"46a814b7-5cfb-4a4a-992b-21fbf7bbef58","tool_call_id":"call_0f42c6d755ff48ad92a92db8","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":199,"prompt_tokens":15075,"total_tokens":15274,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":75,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":199},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":15075}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-d905f71c-22dd-91ed-bc2a-ceb730d4d638","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-b90f-7ec0-9bcf-3d1cdcf52cbc-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取人工复核路由脚本，了解具体的判定逻辑和规则","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/run.py"},"id":"call_58844d1039f6469a9354557d","type":"tool_call"},{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取技能路由器卡片，了解能力边界","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/router_card.json"},"id":"call_efc4de9e0b4848b4a591fcb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":15075,"output_tokens":199,"total_tokens":15274,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":75}}},{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport math\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom hashlib import sha1, sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\ntry:\n    import yaml\nexcept Exception:\n    yaml = None\n\nVERSION = \"1.0.0\"\n\nclass SkillInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Input file could not be loaded; reported through the standard failure contract.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, code: str, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.code = code\n        self.message = message\n\n\ndef argv_output() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort --output path so early input failures still honour it.\"\"\"\n    argv = sys.argv\n    if \"--output\" in argv:\n        index = argv.index(\"--output\")\n        if index + 1 < len(argv):\n            return argv[index + 1]\n    return None\n\n\ndef load_structured(path: str | None) -> Any:\n    if not path:\n        return {}\n    source = Path(path)\n    if not source.exists():\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_NOT_FOUND\", f\"Input file not found: {path}\")\n    if source.is_dir():\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_NOT_FOUND\", f\"Input path is a directory, not a file: {path}\")\n    try:\n        text = source.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError as exc:\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_UNREADABLE\", f\"Could not read input file {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if source.suffix.lower() in {\".yaml\", \".yml\"}:\n        if yaml is None:\n            raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_YAML\", \"PyYAML is required to read YAML files\")\n        try:\n            return yaml.safe_load(text) or {}\n        except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - yaml raises library specific errors\n            raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_YAML\", f\"Invalid YAML in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if not text.strip():\n        return {}\n    try:\n        return json.loads(text)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_JSON\", f\"Invalid JSON in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n\ndef load_config(path: str | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n\ndef load_list(path: str | None, key: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    if isinstance(data, list):\n        return data\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        value = data.get(key) or data.get(\"data\", {}).get(key, [])\n        return value if isinstance(value, list) else []\n    return []\n\ndef load_dict(path: str | None, key: str | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return {}\n    if key and key in data and isinstance(data[key], dict):\n        return data[key]\n    if key and isinstance(data.get(\"data\"), dict) and isinstance(data[\"data\"].get(key), dict):\n        return data[\"data\"][key]\n    return data\n\ndef load_input(path: str | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n\ndef input_value(input_data: dict[str, Any], *keys: str, default: Any = None) -> Any:\n    nested = input_data.get(\"data\") if isinstance(input_data.get(\"data\"), dict) else {}\n    for key in keys:\n        if input_data.get(key) is not None:\n            return input_data[key]\n        if nested.get(key) is not None:\n            return nested[key]\n    return default\n\ndef input_list(input_data: dict[str, Any], key: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    value = input_value(input_data, key, default=[])\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else []\n\ndef input_dict(input_data: dict[str, Any], key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    value = input_value(input_data, key, default={})\n    return value if isinstance(value, dict) else {}\n\ndef parse_json_arg(value: str | None, default: Any) -> Any:\n    return json.loads(value) if value else default\n\ndef success(skill: str, data: dict[str, Any], confidence: float = 1.0) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\"skill\": skill, \"version\": VERSION, \"status\": \"success\", \"confidence\": round(float(confidence), 4), \"data\": data}\n\ndef failed(skill: str, code: str, message: str, retryable: bool = False, detail: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\"skill\": skill, \"version\": VERSION, \"status\": \"failed\", \"error_code\": code, \"message\": message, \"retryable\": retryable, \"detail\": detail or {}}\n\ndef emit(result: dict[str, Any], output: str | None) -> int:\n    text = json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    if output:\n        path = Path(output)\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        path.write_text(text + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(text)\n    return 0 if result.get(\"status\") == \"success\" else 1\n\ndef parse_time(value: str | None, fallback: datetime | None = None) -> datetime:\n    if not value:\n        return fallback or datetime.now().astimezone()\n    return datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n\ndef utc_now_iso() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\ndef iso_add_seconds(value: str, seconds: int | float) -> str:\n    return (parse_time(value) + timedelta(seconds=float(seconds))).isoformat()\n\ndef bbox_center(bbox: list[float]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return ((x1 + x2) / 2, (y1 + y2) / 2)\n\ndef bbox_bottom_center(bbox: list[float]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    x1, _, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return ((x1 + x2) / 2, y2)\n\ndef bbox_area(bbox: list[float]) -> float:\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return max(0.0, x2 - x1) * max(0.0, y2 - y1)\n\ndef bbox_overlap(a: list[float], b: list[float]) -> float:\n    ax1, ay1, ax2, ay2 = a\n    bx1, by1, bx2, by2 = b\n    inter = bbox_area([max(ax1, bx1), max(ay1, by1), min(ax2, bx2), min(ay2, by2)])\n    base = bbox_area(a)\n    return 0.0 if base <= 0 else inter / base\n\ndef polygon_bounds(polygon: list[list[float]]) -> list[float]:\n    xs = [p[0] for p in polygon]\n    ys = [p[1] for p in polygon]\n    return [min(xs), min(ys), max(xs), max(ys)] if xs and ys else [0, 0, 0, 0]\n\ndef polygon_area(polygon: list[list[float]]) -> float:\n    if len(polygon) < 3:\n        return 0.0\n    total = 0.0\n    for i, (x1, y1) in enumerate(polygon):\n        x2, y2 = polygon[(i + 1) % len(polygon)]\n        total += x1 * y2 - x2 * y1\n    return abs(total) / 2\n\ndef point_in_polygon(point: tuple[float, float], polygon: list[list[float]]) -> bool:\n    x, y = point\n    inside = False\n    j = len(polygon) - 1\n    for i, (xi, yi) in enumerate(polygon):\n        xj, yj = polygon[j]\n        if (yi > y) != (yj > y):\n            x_at_y = (xj - xi) * (y - yi) / ((yj - yi) or 1e-9) + xi\n            if x < x_at_y:\n                inside = not inside\n        j = i\n    return inside\n\ndef distance(a: tuple[float, float], b: tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n    return math.hypot(a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1])\n\ndef subject_id(item: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return item.get(\"track_id\") or item.get(\"object_id\") or item.get(\"id\") or \"unknown\"\n\ndef iter_detection_objects(detections: list[dict[str, Any]]):\n    for detection in detections:\n        for obj in detection.get(\"objects\", []):\n            enriched = dict(obj)\n            enriched.setdefault(\"frame_id\", detection.get(\"frame_id\"))\n            enriched.setdefault(\"timestamp\", detection.get(\"timestamp\"))\n            yield enriched\n\nSKILL = \"human-review-routing\"\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Route event candidates to manual review or auto-pass.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--input\", help=\"Optional JSON payload; CLI flags override matching fields.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--event-json\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--camera-health-json\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--review-threshold\", type=float)\n    p.add_argument(\"--config\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--output\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    input_data = load_input(args.input)\n    config = load_config(args.config)\n    event = load_dict(args.event_json, \"event\") if args.event_json else input_dict(input_data, \"event\") or input_data\n    camera_health = load_dict(args.camera_health_json) if args.camera_health_json else input_dict(input_data, \"camera_health\")\n    event_type = event.get(\"event_type\")\n    review_thresholds = config.get(\"review_thresholds\", {})\n    threshold = args.review_threshold if args.review_threshold is not None else float(input_value(input_data, \"review_threshold\", default=review_thresholds.get(event_type, config.get(\"default_review_threshold\", 0.85))))\n    high_risk = set(config.get(\"high_risk_event_types\", []))\n    reasons = []\n    if float(event.get(\"confidence\", 0)) < threshold:\n        reasons.append(\"confidence_below_threshold\")\n    if event.get(\"event_type\") in high_risk:\n        reasons.append(\"high_risk_event_type\")\n    if camera_health.get(\"health_status\") == \"degraded\":\n        reasons.append(\"camera_health_degraded\")\n    if event.get(\"affects_enforcement\"):\n        reasons.append(\"affects_enforcement\")\n    data = {\"event_id\": event.get(\"event_id\"), \"review_required\": bool(reasons), \"reasons\": reasons, \"review_threshold\": threshold, \"queue\": \"manual_review\" if reasons else \"auto_pass\"}\n    return emit(success(SKILL, data), args.output)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        raise SystemExit(main())\n    except SkillInputError as exc:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            emit(\n                {\n                    \"skill\": SKILL,\n                    \"version\": VERSION,\n                    \"status\": \"failed\",\n                    \"error_code\": exc.code,\n                    \"message\": exc.message,\n                    \"retryable\": False,\n                    \"detail\": {},\n                },\n                argv_output(),\n            )\n        )\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"580d15a7-52c6-4db3-8874-9ea4828bb5ce","tool_call_id":"call_58844d1039f6469a9354557d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"id\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"description\": \"Decide whether video event candidates require manual review based on confidence, event type, camera health, and enforcement impact.\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"scenes\": [\"video_surveillance\"],\n    \"is_public\": false,\n    \"task_types\": [\"human_review_routing\"],\n    \"input_types\": [\"event_json\", \"camera_health_json\"],\n    \"output_types\": [\"review_json\"]\n  },\n  \"routing\": {\n    \"routing_text\": \"名称：human-review-routing\\n描述：对 single-video-event-analysis 产生的事件候选做人工复核分流，依据置信度、高风险事件、摄像头健康和执法影响决定 manual_review 或 auto_pass。\\n适合使用：人工复核；低置信度分流；高风险事件分流。\\n不适合使用：生成事件；证据截图。\",\n    \"positive_triggers\": [\"人工复核\", \"review routing\", \"复核队列\", \"低置信度\"],\n    \"negative_triggers\": [\"事件检测\", \"证据截图\"],\n    \"keywords\": [\"review\", \"manual_review\", \"confidence\"],\n    \"anti_keywords\": [\"detect\"]\n  },\n  \"execution\": {\n    \"required_tools\": [\"bash\", \"read_file\"],\n    \"allowed_file_patterns\": [\"*.json\"],\n    \"can_run_standalone\": true\n  },\n  \"routing_policy\": {\n    \"priority\": 72,\n    \"conflict_group\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"prefer_when\": [\"需要人工复核分流\"],\n    \"defer_when\": [\"需要事件分析\"]\n  },\n  \"source\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"skills/custom/human-review-routing\",\n    \"skill_md_path\": \"skills/custom/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"generator_version\": \"manual-llm-event-review-1.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"embedding\": {\"es_doc_id\": \"human-review-routing\"}\n}\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"7380a80f-e5e7-48e6-a134-08844d778284","tool_call_id":"call_efc4de9e0b4848b4a591fcb6","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"根据 `human-review-routing` 技能的实际判定逻辑，以下四类结果**必须进入人工复核**：\n\n---\n\n## 一、置信度低于阈值（`confidence_below_threshold`）\n\n当算法输出的事件置信度低于系统配置的审查阈值时，自动触发复核。\n\n- **默认阈值**：`0.85`（即 85%）\n- **可配置差异化阈值**：通过 `review_thresholds.<event_type>` 对不同类型事件设置不同基线\n- **触发条件**：`event.confidence < threshold`\n\n> 低置信度意味着模型对该事件的判断不够确定，可能是场景复杂、目标部分遮挡或行为不典型导致的误判风险较高。\n\n---\n\n## 二、高风险事件类型（`high_risk_event_type`）\n\n当事件标签被标记为**高风险类型**时，无论置信度高低均需复核。\n\n- 由配置项 `high_risk_event_types` 定义，典型包括：\n  - **打架斗殴**\n  - **人员摔倒**\n  - **烟火/火灾**\n  - **非法入侵**\n  - **交通事故**\n  - 其他可能涉及人身安全的紧急事件\n\n> 高风险事件即使算法判断较确定，也因后果严重性而需要人工二次确认。\n\n---\n\n## 三、摄像头画面质量降级（`camera_health_degraded`）\n\n当关联摄像头的健康状态为 **\"degraded\"** 时，该摄像头产生的所有事件均需复核。\n\n- 覆盖的场景包括：离线、黑屏、模糊、**遮挡（occluded）**、冻结、损坏、画面偏移等\n- 遮挡面积越大、持续时间越长，越可能导致检测不可靠\n\n> 画面被遮挡或质量下降时，算法的检测结果可信度已无法保证，必须人工确认。\n\n---\n\n## 四、涉及执法影响（`affects_enforcement`）\n\n当事件被标记为 **affects_enforcement = true** 时，无条件进入人工复核队列。\n\n- 典型场景：违停取证、闯红灯抓拍、占道经营认定、违章建筑巡查等\n- 这类事件的结果将作为**行政执法证据**使用，合规要求严格\n\n> 执法类事件涉及法律后果和证据链完整性，不能仅依赖算法结论直接处置。\n\n---\n\n## 复核分流结果\n\n满足上述任一条件时，系统将输出：\n\n| 字段 | 值 |\n|------|-----|\n| `review_required` | `true` |\n| `reasons` | 触发的原因列表（可多个） |\n| `queue` | `\"manual_review\"` |\n\n没有任何条件触发时：\n\n| 字段 | 值 |\n|------|-----|\n| `review_required` | `false` |\n| `reasons` | `[]` |\n| `queue` | `\"auto_pass\"` |\n\n---\n\n**总结**：置信度不足、画面被遮挡/质量降级、事件属高风险类型、涉及执法取证——这四条红线中的任意一条命中，结果就必须进入人工复核队列，不得自动放行。","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":841,"prompt_tokens":18352,"total_tokens":19193,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":182,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":841},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":18352}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-eaa04434-7bfd-9b82-8b2d-2d3820f0b7af","finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-c469-76a1-96c0-f085123cb242-0","tool_calls":[],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":18352,"output_tokens":841,"total_tokens":19193,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":182}}}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/31d92145-e0b0-46b4-8190-760bdc99fc9a/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/31d92145-e0b0-46b4-8190-760bdc99fc9a/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/31d92145-e0b0-46b4-8190-760bdc99fc9a/user-data/outputs"},"raw_messages":[{"content":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"f5fe0a5f-0350-4490-8dc7-7f251fb52854"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"fa8651fd-423a-4c6b-b094-c538e3f662f8"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？\n任务规划：\n1. 读取视频监控系统的事件配置表与算法日志，解析当前设定的置信度阈值参数、画面遮挡检测模块的触发逻辑及执法相关事件的自动标记规则，完成数据结构化提取。预期产出：系统触发条件清单与原始参数映射表。\n2. 依托视频监控场景的目标检测与行为识别能力，按置信度低于基线、遮挡面积占比超限、事件标签含执法属性三项维度对告警数据进行过滤与归类，建立分类判定口径。预期产出：分维度的待复核事件特征矩阵。\n3. 检索安防巡检标准作业流程与执法证据留存规范，将分类结果与合规依据进行交叉比对，识别强制复核的边界条件与潜在漏判风险。预期产出：带依据索引的复核规则对照表及合规性校验报告。\n4. 整合校验后的规则清单与操作要求，编排人工复核任务的优先级序列、处置流转路径及溯源字段，生成标准化执行指引文档。预期产出：可落地的强制人工复核任务清单与操作手册。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '', '监控目标': '', '时间范围': '', '输出形式': ''}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"1c29b81c-0454-4ae9-a8b7-1052fa09fb98"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":103,"prompt_tokens":13198,"total_tokens":13301,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":57,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":103},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13198}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-2c832405-2f60-936b-a1c4-5de839c9d8aa","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-7ae7-78b2-9079-32b3ff87d4ea-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_skill","args":{"skill_name":"human-review-routing","mode":"prepare"},"id":"call_e19d9a1a18bd496a895690c2","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13198,"output_tokens":103,"total_tokens":13301,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":57}}},{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"prepared\",\n  \"skill_name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n  \"input_envelope\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"request_id\": \"86bfd1cb-5020-4e7d-8027-98f4b34c69e4\",\n    \"skill_name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"scenario\": \"video_surveillance\",\n    \"capability\": \"skill_invocation\",\n    \"query\": {\n      \"raw\": \"<system_reminder>\\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\\n<hidden_step source=\\\"intent_recognition\\\" title=\\\"意图识别\\\">\\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\\n任务切分：\\n- 事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？\\n任务规划：\\n1. 读取视频监控系统的事件配置表与算法日志，解析当前设定的置信度阈值参数、画面遮挡检测模块的触发逻辑及执法相关事件的自动标记规则，完成数据结构化提取。预期产出：系统触发条件清单与原始参数映射表。\\n2. 依托视频监控场景的目标检测与行为识别能力，按置信度低于基线、遮挡面积占比超限、事件标签含执法属性三项维度对告警数据进行过滤与归类，建立分类判定口径。预期产出：分维度的待复核事件特征矩阵。\\n3. 检索安防巡检标准作业流程与执法证据留存规范，将分类结果与合规依据进行交叉比对，识别强制复核的边界条件与潜在漏判风险。预期产出：带依据索引的复核规则对照表及合规性校验报告。\\n4. 整合校验后的规则清单与操作要求，编排人工复核任务的优先级序列、处置流转路径及溯源字段，生成标准化执行指引文档。预期产出：可落地的强制人工复核任务清单与操作手册。\\n场景任务：\\n- video_surveillance: 我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。\\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '', '监控目标': '', '时间范围': '', '输出形式': ''}\\n任务提示：\\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\\n</hidden_step>\\n</system_reminder>\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"parameters\": {}\n    },\n    \"routing\": {\n      \"selected_skill\": \"human-review-routing\",\n      \"allowed_skills\": [\n        \"analyze-video\",\n        \"batch-video-ingestion\",\n        \"camera-health-check\",\n        \"city-video-intelligence\",\n        \"duplicate-event-merge\",\n        \"evidence-package-generation\",\n        \"evidence-snapshot\",\n        \"ffmpeg-utils\",\n        \"frame-sampling\",\n        \"human-review-routing\",\n        \"object-detection\",\n        \"object-statistics\",\n        \"object-tracking\",\n        \"privacy-masking\",\n        \"roi-mapping\",\n        \"single-video-event-analysis\",\n        \"video-embedding-index\",\n        \"video-object-analytics\",\n        \"video-search\",\n        \"video-segment-extraction\",\n        \"video-stream-ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"selection_owner\": \"lead_agent\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"legacy_invocation\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\",\n    \"skill_file\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"container_skill_file\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"selected_data_sources\": [],\n    \"argv\": [],\n    \"env\": {},\n    \"parameters\": {},\n    \"working_directory\": \"/app/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\",\n    \"adapter_note\": \"Load the returned container_skill_file, follow its SKILL.md workflow, and use selected_data_sources/parameters as the legacy inputs.\"\n  },\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Read container_skill_file before executing the Skill workflow.\",\n    \"Use selected_data_sources and parameters as the legacy inputs.\",\n    \"After execution, call invoke_skill again with mode='wrap_output' to produce SkillResult.\"\n  ]\n}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"invoke_skill","id":"e96e6d94-77c2-4144-a4ee-4ea67b946d5e","tool_call_id":"call_e19d9a1a18bd496a895690c2","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":90,"prompt_tokens":14360,"total_tokens":14450,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":27,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":90},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14360}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-d741c383-7866-992f-9978-ee6e0dc74f8e","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-8299-7dc1-8bf6-8f4d8460b111-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取人工复核路由技能的工作流程文档","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md"},"id":"call_b996362cec4549fc8b681f3a","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14360,"output_tokens":90,"total_tokens":14450,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":27}}},{"content":"---\nname: human-review-routing\ndescription: Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.\n---\n\n# Human Review Routing\n\n## Execution Priority\n\nPrioritize calling this skill's `scripts/run.py` entrypoint first. Only write custom code after the script result is unsuitable or the script cannot cover the requested task.\n\n## Input Resolution\n\nIf event confidence or event fields are missing but the user provided a video analysis request, first call `single-video-event-analysis` to produce candidate events, then call this skill for review routing.\n\n\n## Atomic CLI\n\nRun this skill directly with its own script. The script does not call other skill scripts and does not depend on shared `src`, `tools`, or registry modules.\n\n```bash\npython human-review-routing/scripts/run.py --event-json <event.json> --camera-health-json <health.json> --config <config.json> --output <review.json>\n```\n\nParameters: `--event-json`, `--camera-health-json`, `--review-threshold`, `--config`, `--output`.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Read event confidence, event type, camera health, and review threshold.\n2. Require review for low confidence, high-risk types, degraded cameras, new cameras, or enforcement impact.\n3. Return review flag, reasons, threshold, and queue.\n\n## Available Implementation\n\nThis skill is implemented as an atomic standalone script in its own `scripts/run.py`. The script contains the executable logic for this skill and must not import shared `src`, `tools`, or registry modules.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `event`\n- `camera_health`\n- Optional `review_threshold`\n\nConfig:\n- `default_review_threshold`\n- `review_thresholds.<event_type>`\n- `high_risk_event_types`\n\n## Outputs\n\nReturns `event_id`, `review_required`, `reasons`, `review_threshold`, and `queue`.\n\n## Failure Modes\n\nThe current implementation tolerates missing optional config and falls back to threshold `0.85`.\n\n## Constraints\n\nDo not merge duplicate events or generate evidence.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"9aace99d-8820-4110-a183-f8309d7a205a","tool_call_id":"call_b996362cec4549fc8b681f3a","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":177,"prompt_tokens":14912,"total_tokens":15089,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":120,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":177},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14912}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-e48836b1-7243-9d9e-a191-b6ff0e28a72b","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-aab8-7c00-a3b4-5fff706e1f35-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ls","args":{"description":"查看人工复核技能目录结构","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing"},"id":"call_0f42c6d755ff48ad92a92db8","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":14912,"output_tokens":177,"total_tokens":15089,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":120}}},{"content":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/run.py\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/__pycache__\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\n/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/router_card.json","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"ls","id":"46a814b7-5cfb-4a4a-992b-21fbf7bbef58","tool_call_id":"call_0f42c6d755ff48ad92a92db8","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":199,"prompt_tokens":15075,"total_tokens":15274,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":75,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":199},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":15075}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-d905f71c-22dd-91ed-bc2a-ceb730d4d638","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e23-b90f-7ec0-9bcf-3d1cdcf52cbc-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取人工复核路由脚本，了解具体的判定逻辑和规则","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/scripts/run.py"},"id":"call_58844d1039f6469a9354557d","type":"tool_call"},{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取技能路由器卡片，了解能力边界","path":"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/router_card.json"},"id":"call_efc4de9e0b4848b4a591fcb6","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":15075,"output_tokens":199,"total_tokens":15274,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":75}}},{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport math\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom hashlib import sha1, sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\ntry:\n    import yaml\nexcept Exception:\n    yaml = None\n\nVERSION = \"1.0.0\"\n\nclass SkillInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Input file could not be loaded; reported through the standard failure contract.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, code: str, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.code = code\n        self.message = message\n\n\ndef argv_output() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort --output path so early input failures still honour it.\"\"\"\n    argv = sys.argv\n    if \"--output\" in argv:\n        index = argv.index(\"--output\")\n        if index + 1 < len(argv):\n            return argv[index + 1]\n    return None\n\n\ndef load_structured(path: str | None) -> Any:\n    if not path:\n        return {}\n    source = Path(path)\n    if not source.exists():\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_NOT_FOUND\", f\"Input file not found: {path}\")\n    if source.is_dir():\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_NOT_FOUND\", f\"Input path is a directory, not a file: {path}\")\n    try:\n        text = source.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError as exc:\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_UNREADABLE\", f\"Could not read input file {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if source.suffix.lower() in {\".yaml\", \".yml\"}:\n        if yaml is None:\n            raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_YAML\", \"PyYAML is required to read YAML files\")\n        try:\n            return yaml.safe_load(text) or {}\n        except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - yaml raises library specific errors\n            raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_YAML\", f\"Invalid YAML in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if not text.strip():\n        return {}\n    try:\n        return json.loads(text)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        raise SkillInputError(\"INPUT_INVALID_JSON\", f\"Invalid JSON in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n\ndef load_config(path: str | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n\ndef load_list(path: str | None, key: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    if isinstance(data, list):\n        return data\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        value = data.get(key) or data.get(\"data\", {}).get(key, [])\n        return value if isinstance(value, list) else []\n    return []\n\ndef load_dict(path: str | None, key: str | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return {}\n    if key and key in data and isinstance(data[key], dict):\n        return data[key]\n    if key and isinstance(data.get(\"data\"), dict) and isinstance(data[\"data\"].get(key), dict):\n        return data[\"data\"][key]\n    return data\n\ndef load_input(path: str | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    data = load_structured(path)\n    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n\ndef input_value(input_data: dict[str, Any], *keys: str, default: Any = None) -> Any:\n    nested = input_data.get(\"data\") if isinstance(input_data.get(\"data\"), dict) else {}\n    for key in keys:\n        if input_data.get(key) is not None:\n            return input_data[key]\n        if nested.get(key) is not None:\n            return nested[key]\n    return default\n\ndef input_list(input_data: dict[str, Any], key: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    value = input_value(input_data, key, default=[])\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else []\n\ndef input_dict(input_data: dict[str, Any], key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    value = input_value(input_data, key, default={})\n    return value if isinstance(value, dict) else {}\n\ndef parse_json_arg(value: str | None, default: Any) -> Any:\n    return json.loads(value) if value else default\n\ndef success(skill: str, data: dict[str, Any], confidence: float = 1.0) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\"skill\": skill, \"version\": VERSION, \"status\": \"success\", \"confidence\": round(float(confidence), 4), \"data\": data}\n\ndef failed(skill: str, code: str, message: str, retryable: bool = False, detail: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\"skill\": skill, \"version\": VERSION, \"status\": \"failed\", \"error_code\": code, \"message\": message, \"retryable\": retryable, \"detail\": detail or {}}\n\ndef emit(result: dict[str, Any], output: str | None) -> int:\n    text = json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    if output:\n        path = Path(output)\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        path.write_text(text + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(text)\n    return 0 if result.get(\"status\") == \"success\" else 1\n\ndef parse_time(value: str | None, fallback: datetime | None = None) -> datetime:\n    if not value:\n        return fallback or datetime.now().astimezone()\n    return datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n\ndef utc_now_iso() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\ndef iso_add_seconds(value: str, seconds: int | float) -> str:\n    return (parse_time(value) + timedelta(seconds=float(seconds))).isoformat()\n\ndef bbox_center(bbox: list[float]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return ((x1 + x2) / 2, (y1 + y2) / 2)\n\ndef bbox_bottom_center(bbox: list[float]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    x1, _, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return ((x1 + x2) / 2, y2)\n\ndef bbox_area(bbox: list[float]) -> float:\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = bbox\n    return max(0.0, x2 - x1) * max(0.0, y2 - y1)\n\ndef bbox_overlap(a: list[float], b: list[float]) -> float:\n    ax1, ay1, ax2, ay2 = a\n    bx1, by1, bx2, by2 = b\n    inter = bbox_area([max(ax1, bx1), max(ay1, by1), min(ax2, bx2), min(ay2, by2)])\n    base = bbox_area(a)\n    return 0.0 if base <= 0 else inter / base\n\ndef polygon_bounds(polygon: list[list[float]]) -> list[float]:\n    xs = [p[0] for p in polygon]\n    ys = [p[1] for p in polygon]\n    return [min(xs), min(ys), max(xs), max(ys)] if xs and ys else [0, 0, 0, 0]\n\ndef polygon_area(polygon: list[list[float]]) -> float:\n    if len(polygon) < 3:\n        return 0.0\n    total = 0.0\n    for i, (x1, y1) in enumerate(polygon):\n        x2, y2 = polygon[(i + 1) % len(polygon)]\n        total += x1 * y2 - x2 * y1\n    return abs(total) / 2\n\ndef point_in_polygon(point: tuple[float, float], polygon: list[list[float]]) -> bool:\n    x, y = point\n    inside = False\n    j = len(polygon) - 1\n    for i, (xi, yi) in enumerate(polygon):\n        xj, yj = polygon[j]\n        if (yi > y) != (yj > y):\n            x_at_y = (xj - xi) * (y - yi) / ((yj - yi) or 1e-9) + xi\n            if x < x_at_y:\n                inside = not inside\n        j = i\n    return inside\n\ndef distance(a: tuple[float, float], b: tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n    return math.hypot(a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1])\n\ndef subject_id(item: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return item.get(\"track_id\") or item.get(\"object_id\") or item.get(\"id\") or \"unknown\"\n\ndef iter_detection_objects(detections: list[dict[str, Any]]):\n    for detection in detections:\n        for obj in detection.get(\"objects\", []):\n            enriched = dict(obj)\n            enriched.setdefault(\"frame_id\", detection.get(\"frame_id\"))\n            enriched.setdefault(\"timestamp\", detection.get(\"timestamp\"))\n            yield enriched\n\nSKILL = \"human-review-routing\"\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Route event candidates to manual review or auto-pass.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--input\", help=\"Optional JSON payload; CLI flags override matching fields.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--event-json\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--camera-health-json\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--review-threshold\", type=float)\n    p.add_argument(\"--config\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--output\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    input_data = load_input(args.input)\n    config = load_config(args.config)\n    event = load_dict(args.event_json, \"event\") if args.event_json else input_dict(input_data, \"event\") or input_data\n    camera_health = load_dict(args.camera_health_json) if args.camera_health_json else input_dict(input_data, \"camera_health\")\n    event_type = event.get(\"event_type\")\n    review_thresholds = config.get(\"review_thresholds\", {})\n    threshold = args.review_threshold if args.review_threshold is not None else float(input_value(input_data, \"review_threshold\", default=review_thresholds.get(event_type, config.get(\"default_review_threshold\", 0.85))))\n    high_risk = set(config.get(\"high_risk_event_types\", []))\n    reasons = []\n    if float(event.get(\"confidence\", 0)) < threshold:\n        reasons.append(\"confidence_below_threshold\")\n    if event.get(\"event_type\") in high_risk:\n        reasons.append(\"high_risk_event_type\")\n    if camera_health.get(\"health_status\") == \"degraded\":\n        reasons.append(\"camera_health_degraded\")\n    if event.get(\"affects_enforcement\"):\n        reasons.append(\"affects_enforcement\")\n    data = {\"event_id\": event.get(\"event_id\"), \"review_required\": bool(reasons), \"reasons\": reasons, \"review_threshold\": threshold, \"queue\": \"manual_review\" if reasons else \"auto_pass\"}\n    return emit(success(SKILL, data), args.output)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        raise SystemExit(main())\n    except SkillInputError as exc:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            emit(\n                {\n                    \"skill\": SKILL,\n                    \"version\": VERSION,\n                    \"status\": \"failed\",\n                    \"error_code\": exc.code,\n                    \"message\": exc.message,\n                    \"retryable\": False,\n                    \"detail\": {},\n                },\n                argv_output(),\n            )\n        )\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"580d15a7-52c6-4db3-8874-9ea4828bb5ce","tool_call_id":"call_58844d1039f6469a9354557d","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"id\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"name\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"description\": \"Decide whether video event candidates require manual review based on confidence, event type, camera health, and enforcement impact.\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"scenes\": [\"video_surveillance\"],\n    \"is_public\": false,\n    \"task_types\": [\"human_review_routing\"],\n    \"input_types\": [\"event_json\", \"camera_health_json\"],\n    \"output_types\": [\"review_json\"]\n  },\n  \"routing\": {\n    \"routing_text\": \"名称：human-review-routing\\n描述：对 single-video-event-analysis 产生的事件候选做人工复核分流，依据置信度、高风险事件、摄像头健康和执法影响决定 manual_review 或 auto_pass。\\n适合使用：人工复核；低置信度分流；高风险事件分流。\\n不适合使用：生成事件；证据截图。\",\n    \"positive_triggers\": [\"人工复核\", \"review routing\", \"复核队列\", \"低置信度\"],\n    \"negative_triggers\": [\"事件检测\", \"证据截图\"],\n    \"keywords\": [\"review\", \"manual_review\", \"confidence\"],\n    \"anti_keywords\": [\"detect\"]\n  },\n  \"execution\": {\n    \"required_tools\": [\"bash\", \"read_file\"],\n    \"allowed_file_patterns\": [\"*.json\"],\n    \"can_run_standalone\": true\n  },\n  \"routing_policy\": {\n    \"priority\": 72,\n    \"conflict_group\": \"human-review-routing\",\n    \"prefer_when\": [\"需要人工复核分流\"],\n    \"defer_when\": [\"需要事件分析\"]\n  },\n  \"source\": {\n    \"skill_dir\": \"skills/custom/human-review-routing\",\n    \"skill_md_path\": \"skills/custom/human-review-routing/SKILL.md\",\n    \"generator_version\": \"manual-llm-event-review-1.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"embedding\": {\"es_doc_id\": \"human-review-routing\"}\n}\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"7380a80f-e5e7-48e6-a134-08844d778284","tool_call_id":"call_efc4de9e0b4848b4a591fcb6","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"artifacts":[],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","normalized_query":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","routing_query":"场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance。场景说明：视频监控、摄像头、监控录像、视频流、实时画面、视频帧、卡口、安防巡检、目标检测、行为识别、事件发现和监控告警分析场景。需要识别参数：视频对象、监控目标、时间范围、输出形式。用户原始问题：我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","params":{"视频对象":"","监控目标":"","时间范围":"","输出形式":""},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_7bf4f8","text":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_656511","text":"读取视频监控系统的事件配置表与算法日志，解析当前设定的置信度阈值参数、画面遮挡检测模块的触发逻辑及执法相关事件的自动标记规则，完成数据结构化提取。预期产出：系统触发条件清单与原始参数映射表。"},{"task_span_id":"span_c9a44d","text":"依托视频监控场景的目标检测与行为识别能力，按置信度低于基线、遮挡面积占比超限、事件标签含执法属性三项维度对告警数据进行过滤与归类，建立分类判定口径。预期产出：分维度的待复核事件特征矩阵。"},{"task_span_id":"span_6e0ca0","text":"检索安防巡检标准作业流程与执法证据留存规范，将分类结果与合规依据进行交叉比对，识别强制复核的边界条件与潜在漏判风险。预期产出：带依据索引的复核规则对照表及合规性校验报告。"},{"task_span_id":"span_41a08a","text":"整合校验后的规则清单与操作要求，编排人工复核任务的优先级序列、处置流转路径及溯源字段，生成标准化执行指引文档。预期产出：可落地的强制人工复核任务清单与操作手册。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_fb264d","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。","params":{}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_fb264d","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"我将对事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法的结果进行人工复核。","params":{}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧","提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等","提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:f5fe0a5f-0350-4490-8dc7-7f251fb52854"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"事件置信度低、摄像头画面有遮挡或事件涉及执法时，哪些结果必须进入人工复核？","scene":"video_surveillance","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze-video","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"batch-video-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"camera-health-check","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"city-video-intelligence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"duplicate-event-merge","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-package-generation","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"evidence-snapshot","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"ffmpeg-utils","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"frame-sampling","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"human-review-routing","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-detection","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-statistics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"object-tracking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"privacy-masking","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"roi-mapping","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"single-video-event-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-embedding-index","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-object-analytics","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-search","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-segment-extraction","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"video-stream-ingestion","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","frame-sampling","human-review-routing","object-detection","object-statistics","object-tracking","privacy-masking","roi-mapping","single-video-event-analysis","video-embedding-index","video-object-analytics","video-search","video-segment-extraction","video-stream-ingestion"],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:f5fe0a5f-0350-4490-8dc7-7f251fb52854"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":["analyze-video","batch-video-ingestion","camera-health-check","city-video-intelligence","duplicate-event-merge","evidence-package-generation","evidence-snapshot","ffmpeg-utils","fra